## Don'ts
- ❌ Don't use `PIXI.Graphics` for complex shapes rendered every frame — pre-render to a `RenderTexture` once.
- ❌ Don't use DOM elements for game UI unless absolutely necessary (keep the renderer authoritative).
- ❌ Don't mutate PixiJS objects inside event listeners without guards (check if object is destroyed).
- ❌ Don't skip `.destroy()` — PixiJS has no GC for WebGL textures.
- ❌ Don't use `PIXI.Sprite.from()` shorthand in production — go through `PIXI.Assets`.
- ❌ Don't block the main thread during load — always use async/await with a loading screen.

---

## Versioning Note
These rules target **PixiJS v8**. If using v7, note:
- v7 uses `PIXI.Application` with options in the constructor (not `await app.init()`).
- v7 uses `sprite.interactive = true` instead of `sprite.eventMode = 'static'`.
- v8 removed `PIXI.utils` — use direct imports from `pixi.js`.